# Normalise line endings on checkin. The repo previously carried a mix: files
# created by "ansible-galaxy init" or edited on Windows had CRLF, hand-written
# ones had LF. That made diffs noisy - a one-line change could show up as a
# whole-file rewrite - and it reached the servers, since files under files/ are
# copied verbatim.
#
# text=auto lets git decide per file; eol=lf pins the working-tree ending, so
# everything is LF regardless of the platform doing the checkout.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Belt and braces for the formats in this repo.
*.yml   text eol=lf
*.yaml  text eol=lf
*.j2    text eol=lf
*.cfg   text eol=lf
*.sh    text eol=lf
*.md    text eol=lf
*.rules text eol=lf

# Never touched: an ASCII-armoured key is content, not source.
*.asc   -text
